  "depends_on": [],
  "coupling_notes": [
    "One work package, seven concepts in six clusters (hashing, control-bytes, probing, table, api, iteration). There is no second work package in this workspace, so `depends_on` is empty and `required_guarantees` is empty: a work package may not assume its own output as its own input (P1 hit that as a CG6 'mutual satisfaction is not soundness' cycle -- chainlink #15).",
    "The tightest coupling is the probe sequence's dependence on the table's capacity encoding: BR-PROBESEQ-MASK-001 has to derive `capacity_mask + 1 == (1 << capacity_bits)` from RawTable.C001/C004 to discharge the `ProbeSeq.C001` precondition at RawTable.find -> ProbeSeq.offset. That is the one place where a rehash policy change in RawTable would invalidate a callee obligation rather than just a boundary.",
    "Group probing couples to control bytes twice over: GroupProbe.match_full and match_empty_or_deleted read the H2 tag GroupProbe.load writes, and the same mask drives the free-window query BR-GROUPPROBE-FREE-WINDOW-001. Changing the tag encoding in ControlBytes.C007 breaks both bridges at once.",
    "ControlBytes.clear_dead (rehash) is the only edge that destroys tombstones, so it is the only place a capacity change is observable. It is bridged separately (BR-CONTROLBYTES-CLEARDEAD-001) from set_dead (BR-CONTROLBYTES-SETDEAD-001) precisely so that a rehash-only regression is not confused with a tombstone-marking one.",
    "All 30 non-precondition obligations require verus-deductive-check evidence. The promoted interactions are protocol_class `pairwise` with no trusted assumptions, so `trusted_assumptions` is empty.",
    "The 6 precondition obligations are deliberately NOT in `provided_guarantees`: they are established at the call site and discharged by the bridges, which is the only shape that satisfies bridge G2 (`callee_requirement` must be one of the boundary's own `callee_guarantees`). They appear under `required_preconditions_to_establish`, one entry per bridge -- BR-CONTROLBYTES-CLEARDEAD-001/ControlBytes.C005, BR-CONTROLBYTES-SETDEAD-001/ControlBytes.C003, BR-GROUPPROBE-FREE-WINDOW-001/GroupProbe.C001, BR-GROUPPROBE-WINDOW-001/GroupProbe.C001, BR-PROBESEQ-MASK-001/ProbeSeq.C001, BR-RAWINSERT-NONFULL-001/RawTable.C003 -- so nothing is both provided and required. The obligation id lives in each bridge's own `callee_requirement`, which is where bridge G2 reads it from; the manifest schema's `required_preconditions_to_establish` entry carries only `bridge_id`, `callsite_requirement` and `required_assurance`. See epic #1 #112 for the template disagreement that forces this shape.",
    "EC-1 (promoted) resolves the E-007/E-008 conflict in favour of the per-table seed randomising iteration order, so TableIterator.C004 and SwissTable.C004 are written from E-008 and no obligation here constrains an iteration order.",
    "`gate_integrity` carries the real sha256 of the two ligature-managed witness renderer scripts, recomputed by the generator; G13 verifies both against the installed files. The ligature 1.0-era zero hashes P1 had to remove are never written here.",
    "`provenance.promotion_id` is PROM-SWISSTABLE-VERUS-CORE-001, derived from `cluster` alone by accept-promotion and confirmed against the receipt minted by the Stage 4.5 scratch proof (analysis/ligature/stage4-7/stage45-scratch-proof.txt). `provenance.artifact_set_hash` is the real sha256 of THAT SAME SCRATCH receipt, not of a live-root receipt: no promotion receipt exists on the live root yet, because accept-promotion is pending the operator's batch approval, and the only receipt that exists was minted on a scratch copy whose reliance-policy.md had scratch placeholder values filled in. It is a real hash of a real file, but it is NOT the live-root artifact set. After the operator batch, re-run this generator against the real receipt; until then `promotion_id` and `artifact_set_hash` are the two fields to re-read. `validate-work-package` reports the missing receipt separately as a 10.1/info.",
    "E-010 and E-011 are lifecycle: deferred, so they are in the accepted promotion set as evidence records but assert no constraint; no obligation in this manifest rests on either."
  ],
